				<wikidot:authorName>DrGuin</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>987862</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I'm viewing it as a buildup to the pun at the end. I like it in that context.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-459073#post-1410161</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-459073/scp-1638-j#post-1410161</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 05 Apr 2012 01:30:26 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Zekky</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1338494</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Good point, I'll work on that a bit more tomorrow. I changed the sentence you mentioned to this, hopefully it parses better.</p> <p>&quot;As no progress has been made, the Foundation have thrown in the towel and ceased all searching for the novels.&quot;</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-459073#post-1410153</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-459073/scp-1638-j#post-1410153</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 05 Apr 2012 01:04:01 +0000</pubDate>
								<wikidot:authorUserId>1316614</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>I like it, but there are several places where your phrasing is awkward&#8212;the joke is good but you should work on making the cliches flow naturally. Phrases like &quot;The foundation has thrown in the towel with regards to searching for it&quot; are clumsy in the extreme.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-459073#post-1410151</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-459073/scp-1638-j#post-1410151</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 05 Apr 2012 00:57:40 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Zekky</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1338494</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Essentially it's an object that makes people use cliched idioms in their writing as you said. The advertisements are examples of extremely cliched plots. I thought it could be amusing despite being a fairly simple idea.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-459073#post-1410148</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
